* ============================================================================
* Section VII (Deliverable): SQUID‑tunable resonator with injected flux noise
* Target: demonstrate frequency‑jitter PSD and linewidth broadening from flux noise
*
* Notes:
* - This uses JoSIM SPICE‑like syntax and output controls (.tran, .file, .print) per JoSIM docs. citeturn15view0turn18view0
* - Flux noise is injected via a Phase Source whose SOURCETYPE is your new FNOISE(...) (JoSIM‑Pro).
* - DC bias + noise are implemented as TWO phase sources in series so we don't need expression support inside devices.
* - Adjust parameters to your preferred operating point and simulation runtime.
* ============================================================================

* ---------- Global parameters (all expressions must be in .param) ----------
.option seed=123456789

* Bias point (choose a smooth point away from half‑flux singularities)
* PHI_BIAS_FRAC is Φbias / Φ0 (dimensionless fraction of a flux quantum)
.param PHI_BIAS_FRAC=0.25
.param PHI0=PHI_ZERO

* Convert Φbias to an equivalent PHASE source value (radians): φbias = 2π * Φbias/Φ0
.param PHASE_BIAS= (2*PI*PHI_BIAS_FRAC)

* Josephson junction model parameters (scaled example; tune to taste)
* For a numerically friendly demo (lower resonator frequency), you may pick very small Ic to enlarge Lj.
.param IC=1.0e-8
.param RN=10.0
.param CAPJ=2.0e-13

* DC SQUID loop inductance (keep small for βL << 1 if you want the simple analytic comparator)
.param L_LOOP=2.0e-10

* Resonator (choose values so f0 is manageable for long transient runs)
.param C_RES=1.0e-10
.param R_DAMP=2.0e3

* Excitation: a short current impulse to start ring‑down
.param I_PULSE=2.0e-6
.param T_RISE =1.0e-10
.param T_FALL =1.0e-10
.param T_WIDTH=3.0e-9

* Flux noise (FNOISE) parameters
* A_PHI1 is ASD at 1 Hz in units of Φ0/sqrt(Hz) (as used in your paper)
.param A_PHI1 =2.0e-6
.param ALPHA  =1.0
.param TD     =1.0e-6
.param DTNOISE =1.0e-8
.param TCORR  =1.0e-6
.param N_OU   =48

* ---------- JJ model ----------
.model JJMOD jj(ic=IC r0=RN cap=CAPJ)

* ---------- Circuit ----------
* Resonator node
* SQUID sits from NRES to ground, made of two JJs whose lower electrodes are split (0 and NLOOP)
* with a superconducting link (L_LOOP) and an imposed external phase (bias + noise).

* Resonator tank
CRES  NRES 0    C_RES
RDMP  NRES 0    R_DAMP

* SQUID junctions
* JoSIM JJ syntax: B<label> N+ N- PhaseNode MODEL citeturn1view1
BJJ1  NRES 0     NRES JJMOD
BJJ2  NRES NLOOP NRES JJMOD

* External flux implemented as phase (φ = 2π Φ/Φ0) in series with loop inductance.
PBIAS  0     NPHI   DC  PHASE_BIAS
PNFLUX NPHI  NPHI2  FNOISE(A_PHI1 ALPHA TD DTNOISE TCORR N_OU)
LLOOP  NPHI2 NLOOP  L_LOOP

* Kick the resonator (current pulse)
IKICK NRES 0 PULSE(0 I_PULSE 0 T_RISE T_FALL T_WIDTH)

* ---------- Transient + output ----------
* .tran TSTEP TSTOP [PSTART [PSTEP [PWINDOW]]] [DST] citeturn15view0
* Choose TSTEP small enough to resolve the resonator; PSTEP can decimate output if needed.
.tran 5.0e-11 2.0e-3 0 5.0e-11 0

.file sec7_traces.csv
.print v(NRES) p(PBIAS) p(PNFLUX)

.end